Q4. Starvation Debugging
Answer
Queue Structure
Q1 → Interactive (Highest Priority)

Q2 → System

Q3 → Batch (FCFS)

P5 belongs to Q3
Debug Analysis
Process P5 is placed in Q3 (Batch Queue).
The scheduler always gives priority to Q1 and Q2.
New interactive and system processes continuously arrive in the higher-priority queues.
As a result, P5 never gets CPU time and remains in the ready state indefinitely.
Root Cause
Q1 Processes
      ↓
Executed First
      ↓
Q2 Processes
      ↓
Executed Next
      ↓
P5 in Q3
      ↓
Never Gets CPU Time
      ↓
Starvation
Optimization
Use Aging
Gradually increase the priority of processes that wait for a long time.
Eventually, P5 is promoted to a higher-priority queue and gets CPU time.
Result
Starvation Eliminated

Fair CPU Allocation

Improved System Performance
